WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.375
Expert performance is built through practice that resembles the demands of real work while

00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:05.985
still creating room for improvement.

00:00:05.985 --> 00:00:10.280
Deliberate practice starts with a specific capability, a clear standard, focused effort,

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.685
feedback, and correction.

00:00:11.685 --> 00:00:13.680
It is not just doing the job again and again.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.220
It is designing repetition so weak points become visible and fixable.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.730
Scenario training, simulations, rehearsal, drills, worked examples,

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.255
and edge-case practice all serve different purposes.

00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:25.920
A worked example shows how a strong performer thinks.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.650
A drill strengthens one component.

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.635
A simulation combines components under realistic constraints.

00:00:30.635 --> 00:00:34.185
Edge-case practice teaches the performer what changes when the usual pattern is

00:00:34.185 --> 00:00:34.690
incomplete,

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:35.840
misleading, or missing.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.005
Repetition with variation is important.

00:00:38.005 --> 00:00:41.200
Exact repetition can build fluency, but variation supports transfer.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.435
Change the time pressure, available information, stakeholder, tool failure, handoff point,

00:00:45.435 --> 00:00:46.080
or exception.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.040
The learner must recognize the underlying principle instead of memorizing one scenario.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.340
This helps reduce brittle performance that only works in a familiar example.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.970
Practice should be separated from production when possible.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.565
Production work rewards finishing.

00:00:57.565 --> 00:00:59.075
Practice rewards improving.

00:00:59.075 --> 00:01:02.575
A good practice system gives people permission to slow down, repeat, compare,

00:01:02.575 --> 00:01:05.080
and receive feedback before returning to live work.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.975
The final test is transfer: does the practice make real performance more reliable,

00:01:08.975 --> 00:01:10.720
adaptable, and evidence-informed?
